<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador sells $48 million zero-coupon bonds.</title>
<headline>Ecuador sells $48 million zero-coupon bonds.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador said it sold Tuesday $48 million in 357-day zero-coupon bonds, in an auction held simultaneously on the Quito and Guayaquil stock exchanges.</p>
<p>The bonds were sold at an average discount price of 91.94 percent and an average yield of 8.83 percent.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said it received bids for a total of $254.73 million.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429))</p>
